BabelArena
==========

This repository redistributes four existing agent benchmarks, each extended
with multilingual task data. The evaluation code and task content are the work
of their upstream authors; what is added here is the multilingual data, the
frozen `standard` task subsets, and the unified runner.


benchmarks/tau3/
----------------
Derived from tau2-bench (tau3-bench) by Sierra Research.
    https://github.com/sierra-research/tau2-bench
Licensed under the MIT License; see benchmarks/tau3/LICENSE.

Papers to cite are listed in the Citation section of the top-level README.md
(tau-bench, tau^2-bench, tau-Knowledge, tau-Voice, and the SABER task-fix work).

Modifications in this distribution:
  - Translated policies, tasks, tool descriptions, databases, and user-simulator
    prompts for 23 languages. (Partial German artifacts carried in the source
    tree had no localized database behind them and were dropped.)
  - A frozen `standard` task subset (data/task_subsets/standard/), default.
  - LLM calls go through src/tau2/utils/llm_utils.py, an OpenAI-compatible HTTP
    client, rather than upstream's litellm path.
  - Voice-mode task data and audio assets removed; upstream's shipped baseline
    result archive removed; the translation tooling under tools/ removed.


benchmarks/vitabench/
---------------------
Derived from VitaBench by Meituan LongCat.
    https://github.com/meituan-longcat/vitabench
See benchmarks/vitabench/LICENSE.

    NOTE: the LICENSE file carried in the upstream tree names Sierra Research,
    reflecting that VitaBench adapted part of the tau2-bench codebase. Confirm
    with the VitaBench authors which copyright line should apply to a
    redistribution before publishing.

Modifications in this distribution:
  - Translated tasks, tool schemas, and evaluator prompts for 23 languages.
  - A frozen `standard` task subset (data/task_subsets/standard/), made the
    default in src/vita/cli.py.
  - src/vita/utils/utils.py: DATA_DIR now honours a VITA_DATA_DIR environment
    variable, modelled on tau3's existing TAU2_DATA_DIR, so the data can live
    outside the source tree.
  - src/vita/utils/llm_utils.py: developer comments translated to English, and
    a fix so that an "empty turn" response (thinking only, no content and no
    named tool call) is not written to the request cache -- caching it made
    every retry of that task replay the same dead turn.


benchmarks/deepplanning/
------------------------
Derived from DeepPlanning by the Qwen team.
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/Qwen/DeepPlanning

    *** UNRESOLVED: no license file. ***

    The upstream tree ships no LICENSE, and its README defers to "individual
    domain directories", which also contain none. The license terms for the
    DeepPlanning code and data must be established with the Qwen team before
    this suite is published. Until then, treat benchmarks/deepplanning/ as
    not cleared for redistribution.

Modifications in this distribution:
  - Translated queries, tool schemas, prompts, and per-language rendered seed
    databases for 23 languages.
  - A frozen `standard` task subset (task_subsets/standard/), default.
  - The translation and database-rendering pipeline (translation/, and the
    build scripts under scripts/) removed; documentation updated accordingly.
  - New data_paths.py resolves seed-database locations through a
    DEEPPLANNING_DATA_DIR environment variable (default: in-tree, as upstream),
    so the databases can live outside the source tree. travelplanning/run.py,
    shoppingplanning/run.py, shoppingplanning/run.sh and task_selection.py were
    updated to go through it.
  - run_all.sh accepts DEEPPLANNING_MODELS_CONFIG in its preflight check, not
    only an in-tree models_config.json.
  - travelplanning/run.sh: exits non-zero when a model failed. It counted and
    printed failures but still exited 0, so run_all.sh reported the domain as
    completed and any wrapper above it saw a successful run that had produced no
    results.
  - travelplanning/run.sh: honours DEEPPLANNING_TASK_IDS (as the shopping runner
    already did) and TRAVEL_CONVERSION_MODEL, whose value was previously ignored
    in favour of a hardcoded conversion model.
  - shoppingplanning/run.sh: resumes inside a DEEPPLANNING_RUN_DIR. A level that
    already has its summary is skipped, one whose inference finished is only
    re-evaluated, and any other leftovers are cleared and the level redone.
    Previously any existing output aborted the script, so an interrupted run
    could not be completed under the same directory.


benchmarks/claw/
----------------
Derived from Claw-Eval by Bowen Ye, Rang Li et al.
    https://claw-eval.github.io  (arXiv 2604.06132)
Claw-Eval's tasks draw from and adapt tasks contributed by OpenClaw,
PinchBench, OfficeQA, OneMillion-Bench, Finance Agent and Terminal-Bench 2.0.

    *** UNRESOLVED: no license file. ***

    Upstream's README declares the MIT License and links a LICENSE file, but none is
    present in this tree or anywhere in the history of the fork it was copied
    from. Obtain upstream's LICENSE and copyright line before publishing.

Modifications in this distribution (details: benchmarks/claw/VENDORED.md):
  - Task prompts, fixtures, graders and user-simulator prompts for 23
    languages, and a frozen `standard` task subset (task_subsets/standard/).
  - An Anthropic Messages agent provider (anthropic_native.py), a Gemini
    generateContent route for the user simulator, a reasoning echo switch,
    fail-fast on oversized judge requests, and an optional time-limit
    multiplier (CLAW_EVAL_TIMEOUT_MULT, default off).
  - Local credentials, internal per-model run configs, an internal results log,
    one-off sweep scripts, the failure-analysis module and the translation
    tooling removed.


Third-party models
------------------
Running this suite calls external model APIs. Nothing here grants rights to any
model; the terms of whichever endpoint you configure apply.
